# ─── Connecting the front end to Adminium ────────────────────────────────────
#
# BOTH ARE READ AT BUILD TIME, not at run time. Vite inlines them into the
# bundle, so setting either after a build does nothing until the next one.
#
# Leave them empty and the app builds the demo: Lumen Studio held in the page.
# That is what the adminium.dev demo serves. It is not what you want on your own
# domain, because nothing in it can be edited, exported or kept.
#
# Set them to build the booking pages for their own domain, talking to an
# Adminium somewhere else. Mint the key in Studio -> Public API.
#
# An app installed in Adminium needs neither: Adminium serves its pages and tells
# them their address and keys.
#
# The key is public by design (`adm_pub_`): it selects a scope, reads only what
# that scope lists, and is refused outside /api/v1/public. A secret `adm_sk_`
# key here would be a real leak.
VITE_ADMINIUM_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_ADMINIUM_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
